ChatGPT said:
Absolutely. Your project is already well structured. One small correction: your .gitignore patterns can be simplified, and the README should explicitly state that sel[1:0] maps to in[0]–in[3].

I’d recommend this repository name:

vivado-4to1-mux-structural

GitHub description:

Structural Verilog implementation of a 4:1 MUX using three 2:1 MUXes in Xilinx Vivado, with RTL schematic and behavioral simulation.

Here are clean, ready-to-paste versions of both files.

.gitignore
# ==============================================================================
# Xilinx Vivado Project - Git Ignore
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
